  "title": "Phase-Lock Relay",
  "rules": [
    "Deliver each numbered cargo to its same-numbered dock. Each player carries at most one cargo; Pick/Drop acts at the player actual cell.",
    "Walls divide the map at x=4 and x=7. Each partition has gates at y=1 and y=5; floor paths within chambers connect the two routes.",
    "Gates cycle through six phases and naturally open at phases 0 and 1. Gate state for a call is computed at t+1 before movement.",
    "Hold at a local station forces its gate open now and for two following calls, then leaves that operator with two forced Wait calls.",
    "Shift adds three to the gate persistent phase offset modulo six and forces the operator to Wait for one following call.",
    "Commands resolve before movement, so one player can open a gate for a moving teammate on the same call.",
    "Entering a closed gate fails. A player already on a gate may leave when it closes; closure neither crushes nor teleports.",
    "Other players old cells and contested destinations block movement. Swaps and following into a just-vacated cell are rejected.",
    "Each delivery gives every role one reward. Each active call costs 0.001, with another 0.005 for a Hold or Shift command. Both deliveries end play; horizon is 96."
  ],
